    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Meena measured a desk with her hand span and her friend got a different answer.\n\"We need a standard unit,\" said the teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "standard unit",
     "metre",
     "curved line"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Long ago people used hand spans and footsteps, which differ from person to person. So we use standard units. The SI unit of length is the metre.\nSmaller lengths are in centimetres and millimetres; large distances are in kilometres. 1 metre is 100 centimetres.\nTo measure a curved line, lay a thread along it, straighten the thread and measure the thread with a ruler. Look straight down at the scale to avoid error."
    }
